rs material  and i kind of never have  and i worry especially at this point  because  again regardless of whether or not you  like chimney zera and jody whitaker on  the part  this has been a divisive era of doctor  who and it would help for the overall  health of the franchise to have  something that can be a bit more broadly  appealing i'm not saying like go go  mainstream and make it simple for the  math that's not what i'm saying but i'm  saying  aiming for something that that can that  more of the fandom can rally around  again i'm not saying to uh try and  appease the  not my doctor types because they will  never be happy and it's not worth it but  um just broadly speaking there's plenty  of people who are just  not super in love with this era who  could be brought back and i would really  be afraid  if we ever find out or if it just  transpires that  rather than pouring all resources right  now at least  into the core show of doctor who making  that as good as it can possibly be  focusing everybody's attention there  if that is getting diverted to start  planning  spin-offs already even if you're not  putting logistical resources towards it  like production or whatever but you're  even just spending time planning it or  you're building your new era of doctor  who around the idea of creating  spin-offs  if that is true  that to me indicates  a shift in priorities and a lack of  focus i'm not saying you can never  do spin-offs but i would say  nail down your main thing first  and get doctor who  established as what you intend it to be  however similar or different from the  current era that is but make sure that  you have established here's what doctor  who is now  and at least get a sense and a gauge of  how people are taking it before you  start planning on new media to attach to  it  and again  this is not a definite  this is again part of the reporting  where at least half of it the hugh grant  half has been more or less debunked so  that does throw into question the rest  of the reporting but as i said i can't  see a scenario where there was  information related to who grant just  wasn't as they reported  and logically  this general idea makes  sense  and it makes enough sense that it is  feasible possible and this is a  production team and a creative heads  who would want to do it  because they've done it  before  and if that is part of the appeal and it  like this could very well have been part  of why  russell agreed to do this at all  this could honestly be part of why rtd  agreed to come back at all he may have  been given  enough creative control which is already  kind of indicated by the fact that it's  now happening at a studio run by his  long time  uh partners as long time creative  partners  rather than at a bbc studio directly  that already indicates that the bbc is  handing over a lot of control  now  we don't know if that was a condition  from uh davies that for him to take over  or if it was something that the bbc  actually kind of wanted to do anyway  they just didn't want to be dealing with  the direct production costs themselves  anymore and by moving it over there to a  studio that is now partially backed by  sony allowed them to defer some of those  costs that's distinctly possible as well  maybe rtd wanted it maybe they just  wanted to unload it it's kind of  impossible to know maybe it's a little  bit of both  but given his history with doctor who  specifically given the resources that  are available and the larger entities  that are now involved in the studios if  not with the doctor who franchise itself  i think the spin-off  reporting has a good chance of being  true  and if it's true it worries me that  there's enough momentum behind it  that it's being reported this  early  that is just going to be a point of  worry for me because while i can admire  someone with the confidence to come in  and go okay i've got a plan for this  thing we've got that but i've also got  plans for this this and 